### Ping — happy path (known tenant)
# Verifies the tenant filter resolves a known tenant and lets the request through.
GET {{baseUrl}}/ping
X-Tenant-Id: acme

### Ping — missing tenant (expects 400)
# No X-Tenant-Id header at all -> tenant filter should throw MissingTenantException -> 400 Problem+JSON
GET {{baseUrl}}/ping

### Ping — unknown tenant (expects 401)
# X-Tenant-Id set to a value that doesn't resolve to a real tenant -> UnknownTenantException -> 401 Problem+JSON
GET {{baseUrl}}/ping
X-Tenant-Id: does-not-exist

### Show request/response with MDC requestId echoed in errors (trigger a 401)
# Same as above, but the point of this one is to inspect the Problem+JSON body
# and confirm "requestId" in the response matches the requestId in the server logs (MDC).
GET {{baseUrl}}/ping
X-Tenant-Id: does-not-exist

### OpenAPI JSON - public group
GET {{baseUrl}}/v3/api-docs

### Swagger UI
GET {{baseUrl}}/swagger-ui/index.html

### Example: product list (placeholder for later endpoints; keeps header wiring handy)
# Not implemented yet (catalog API is backlog item after DTOs/validation) — kept here
# so the X-Tenant-Id wiring pattern is ready to copy once /api/products exists.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products
X-Tenant-Id: acme
